From 1bf44a1dd95dd950e5f959c483092e48898aaac6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miyu <miyu@local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:36:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] screencasting: advertise SHM to portal clients and bound the
 frame rate

Screen sharing with xdg-desktop-portal under niri fails for Electron-based
clients (QQ, Feishu, ...) in two ways:

1. They cannot import DMA-BUF, so niri has to offer a shm format explicitly.
   Without a VideoModifier the format is read as a plain linear dmabuf and
   rejected with "no more input formats".

2. niri exposed neither AvailableSourceTypes nor AvailableCursorModes on
   org.gnome.Mutter.ScreenCast, so xdg-desktop-portal-gnome reported zero
   capabilities and rejected every SelectSources call.

Also bound what the screencast stream produces. VideoFramerate 0/1 means
"unlimited" to PipeWire and makes it push frames at the output refresh rate,
which a software H.264 encoder cannot drain; the leftover raw frames
accumulated as shmem until the desktop froze.

- make_video_params: restore upstream dmabuf/shm split, advertise
  VideoModifier=Invalid for the shm-only case, cap framerate to 30 fps.
- make_video_params_shm: shm variant of the above.
- on_add_buffer: evict the oldest shm buffer past 32 entries so a client
  that never drains the stream cannot grow the pool without bound.
- mutter_screen_cast: add AvailableSourceTypes and AvailableCursorModes.
---
 src/dbus/mutter_screen_cast.rs |  24 ++++
 src/screencasting/pw_utils.rs  | 207 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 222 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

